WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:05.379
Many actors are willing to transform themselves
for roles, from gaining and losing weight,

00:00:05.379 --> 00:00:10.710
to wearing prosthetics, and more. But for
some actors, taking on the ultimate film role

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:15.959
means going to extremes — sometimes even
permanently hurting their bodies in the process.

00:00:15.959 --> 00:00:21.610
Here are some actors who've earned some serious,
albeit sometimes invisible, scars for their

00:00:21.610 --> 00:00:22.610
art.

00:00:22.610 --> 00:00:24.760
Jared Leto in Chapter 27

00:00:24.760 --> 00:00:29.490
As we've come to know very well at this point,
Jared Leto is a method actor who doesn't hold

00:00:29.490 --> 00:00:34.410
back when it comes to transforming his body.
He's lost major weight for films such as Requiem

00:00:34.410 --> 00:00:39.570
for a Dream and his Oscar-winning turn in
Dallas Buyers Club. But it was actually gaining

00:00:39.570 --> 00:00:45.501
weight for the 2007 indie film Chapter 27
that really did a number on the actor. Playing

00:00:45.501 --> 00:00:50.500
Mark Chapman, the man who shot and killed
John Lennon, Leto admitted he gained so much

00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:53.900
weight so abruptly that he suffered gout.

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:57.690
Leto revealed that the weight gain hurt his
body so much, towards the end he couldn't

00:00:57.690 --> 00:01:03.130
even walk. He told The Los Angeles Times,
"I had a definite problem with my feet. Towards

00:01:03.130 --> 00:01:07.409
the end of the shoot, one of the glaring issues
was the pain I had with my feet. I couldn't

00:01:07.409 --> 00:01:12.350
walk for long distances. I had a wheelchair
because it was so painful. My body was in

00:01:12.350 --> 00:01:16.350
shock from the amount of weight I gained.
It took about a year to get back to a place

00:01:16.350 --> 00:01:21.399
that felt semi-normal. I don't know if I'll
ever be back to the place I was physically."

00:01:21.399 --> 00:01:25.829
Hey, at least dying his hair green and putting
in metal teeth to play the Joker in Suicide

00:01:25.829 --> 00:01:30.960
Squad left no indelible marks — well except
for on his career.

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:36.959
"I'm just gonna hurt you really really bad."

00:01:36.959 --> 00:01:40.069
Tom Hanks in Philadelphia and Cast Away

00:01:40.069 --> 00:01:44.709
The affable Tom Hanks isn't necessarily known
to be one of those actors who loses himself

00:01:44.709 --> 00:01:49.649
in roles, but he has gone to a few extremes
here and there — and has won two Oscars

00:01:49.649 --> 00:01:55.719
for his efforts. In both the 1993 drama Philadelphia,
in which he plays a lawyer diagnosed with

00:01:55.719 --> 00:02:01.159
AIDS, and the 2000 survival pic Cast Away,
Hanks had to lose a lot of weight during the

00:02:01.159 --> 00:02:02.159
shoot.

00:02:02.159 --> 00:02:05.889
Thanks to the forced fluctuation, and his
own genetics of course, the actor revealed

00:02:05.889 --> 00:02:12.159
that he was later diagnosed with Type 2 Diabetes.
He said that he probably won't be taking on

00:02:12.159 --> 00:02:18.690
any more roles which require him to drastically
change his size as a result of these experiences.

00:02:18.690 --> 00:02:20.670
George Clooney in Syriana

00:02:20.670 --> 00:02:24.549
While George Clooney didn't have to undergo
much of a physical transformation for his

00:02:24.549 --> 00:02:30.250
Oscar-winning role in 2005's Syriana, he still
experienced a real headache during the making

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:34.490
of the movie. While filming a torture scene
for the political thriller, the actor cracked

00:02:34.490 --> 00:02:38.519
his head open during a stunt and severely
injured his spine.

00:02:38.519 --> 00:02:42.750
He told Rolling Stone at the time that the
pain from the injury was so bad, he considered

00:02:42.750 --> 00:02:49.040
taking his own life. "I was at a point where
I thought, 'I can't exist like this. I can't

00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:54.379
actually live.' I was lying in a hospital
bed with an IV in my arm, unable to move,

00:02:54.379 --> 00:02:58.950
having these headaches where it feels like
you're having a stroke, and for a short three-week

00:02:58.950 --> 00:03:03.810
period, I started to think, 'I may have to
do something drastic about this.'"

00:03:03.810 --> 00:03:08.439
Doctors couldn't quite pinpoint where the
injury was at first — they clearly weren't

00:03:08.439 --> 00:03:14.409
as good as his ER alter ego, Doug Ross — but
finally noticed fluid leaking from Clooney's

00:03:14.409 --> 00:03:18.780
spine, and realized that the condition was
more serious than anyone had thought. The

00:03:18.780 --> 00:03:23.650
actor revealed to The Hollywood Reporter that
he was forced to take strong pain medication

00:03:23.650 --> 00:03:28.939
as part of a long process and eventually turned
to pain management for help dealing with his

00:03:28.939 --> 00:03:35.629
chronic discomfort. But he'll never again
be 100 percent. "I've gone from where I can't

00:03:35.629 --> 00:03:40.379
function… to, 'I've got a bad headache'…
My ears will literally pop and my head goes

00:03:40.380 --> 00:03:42.650
apes***. But I'm scrappy."

00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:47.480
"I'm not kidding because I think I've crossed
the line"

00:03:47.480 --> 00:03:50.340
Sylvester Stallone in The Expendables 3

00:03:50.340 --> 00:03:54.690
As a longtime action movie star, Sylvester
Stallone knows a thing or two about cuts,

00:03:54.690 --> 00:03:59.230
bruises, broken bones — the whole shebang.
In fact, he once joked that he grades the

00:03:59.230 --> 00:04:04.510
quality of his movies by how badly he got
hurt making them. So, sufficed it to say,

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:09.280
he's certainly experienced more than his fair
share of pain on the set of movies, including

00:04:09.280 --> 00:04:14.780
a permanent injury on the set of The Expendables
3, in which he reprised his role as mercenary

00:04:14.780 --> 00:04:21.220
Barney Ross. The action star suffered a nasty
fall on the set that left him in need of spinal

00:04:21.220 --> 00:04:22.220
surgery.

00:04:22.220 --> 00:04:23.220
"That hurts"

00:04:23.220 --> 00:04:27.670
But believe it or not, Stallone's injuries
weren't even the scariest from that film set.

00:04:27.670 --> 00:04:32.420
Co-star Jason Statham almost lost his life
during production: while he was driving a

00:04:32.420 --> 00:04:38.640
truck on a loading dock, the brakes failed
and the truck plunged 60 feet into the Black

00:04:38.640 --> 00:04:45.670
Sea. Thankfully, Statham — who once competed
as an Olympic diver — was able to get free

00:04:45.670 --> 00:04:50.420
and swim to safety. And here you thought those
shoot-'em-up-bang-bang blockbusters were totally

00:04:50.420 --> 00:04:51.720
just pretend.

00:04:51.720 --> 00:04:54.490
Linda Hamilton in Terminator 2: Judgment Day

00:04:54.490 --> 00:04:59.990
Linda Hamilton's badass turn as Sarah Connor
in 1991's Terminator 2 set a precedent for

00:04:59.990 --> 00:05:05.100
female action stars to follow. She took the
role very seriously, training her tail off

00:05:05.100 --> 00:05:09.920
to play the hardcore mother of the leader
of the future world. But for all the fight

00:05:09.920 --> 00:05:15.170
sequences and stunt work, it's hard to bounce
back when a shotgun blast goes off near your

00:05:15.170 --> 00:05:19.210
ear. While shooting the scene in which Sarah
is trying to escape the psych ward and has

00:05:19.210 --> 00:05:24.260
to reluctantly accept help from the new and
improved Terminator, the actress forgot to

00:05:24.260 --> 00:05:30.080
put her earplugs back in after a take. When
Schwarzenegger let off a round in the elevator,

00:05:30.080 --> 00:05:36.070
trying to stop the T-1000, the amplified sound
caused Hamilton permanent hearing loss. Of

00:05:36.070 --> 00:05:40.880
course, Hamilton wasn't the first action star
to get hurt from guns shooting blanks.

00:05:40.880 --> 00:05:42.630
Bruce Willis in Die Hard

00:05:42.630 --> 00:05:47.620
That's right: the same type of injury also
befell the man who played John McClaine while

00:05:47.620 --> 00:05:52.710
he was making his action thriller breakthrough,
Die Hard. According to the actor, after firing

00:05:52.710 --> 00:05:57.771
off a fateful round, he suffered "two-thirds
partial hearing loss" in his left ear. He

00:05:57.771 --> 00:06:03.290
added that now has the "tendency to say, 'Whaaa?'"
His daughter Rumer Willis even said the reason

00:06:03.290 --> 00:06:07.760
her dad isn't as talkative while promoting
a movie is because he sometimes struggles

00:06:07.760 --> 00:06:11.940
to hear the questions. That explains a lot.
Or...does it?

00:06:12.700 --> 00:06:13.700
"He's …"

00:06:13.700 --> 00:06:15.370
"I dreamed I was on a boat"

00:06:15.370 --> 00:06:19.070
Michelle Yeoh in Crouching Tiger, Hidden Dragon

00:06:19.070 --> 00:06:24.490
It comes as no surprise that Michelle Yeoh
injured herself during the spectacular Crouching

00:06:24.490 --> 00:06:29.130
Tiger, Hidden Dragon. With all the incredible
stunt choreography involved, there had to

00:06:29.130 --> 00:06:30.420
be a misstep.

00:06:30.420 --> 00:06:35.740
"I think in life you must make a choice. Either
you do it or you don't."

00:06:35.740 --> 00:06:41.110
Indeed, at one point during filming, Yeoh
landed wrong and her knee gave out. Sure enough,

00:06:41.110 --> 00:06:47.190
the action star completely tore an ACL in
her knee. Yeoh had to have surgery and months

00:06:47.190 --> 00:06:52.090
of physical therapy. And while she was able
to recover, she admitted, "You never get all

00:06:52.090 --> 00:06:54.670
the way back to what it was."

00:06:54.670 --> 00:06:57.130
Angelina Jolie in Salt

00:06:57.130 --> 00:07:02.280
Angelina Jolie is another star who never does
any of her action movies half-assed — especially

00:07:02.280 --> 00:07:09.150
her 2010 spy thriller Salt. Jolie played a
CIA officer accused of being a Russian spy

00:07:09.150 --> 00:07:13.950
who must prove her innocence while on the
run. To prep for fight scenes, Jolie had to

00:07:13.950 --> 00:07:18.920
learn a combination of Muay Thai and Krav
Maga, which she did during two-hour sessions

00:07:18.920 --> 00:07:23.840
three to four times a week. Some of her stunts
included jumping off a highway underpass onto

00:07:23.840 --> 00:07:29.240
a moving truck. But amazingly, that wasn't
the scene that literally scarred her for life.

00:07:29.240 --> 00:07:33.830
Speaking at Comic-Con at the time, she said
it happened during a scene which involved

00:07:33.830 --> 00:07:39.280
her rolling onto the floor — and left her
with a permanent scar. Her stunt trainer Simon

00:07:39.280 --> 00:07:44.210
Crane told Us Weekly, "During her final fight
with Liev [Schrieber] … She had to dive

00:07:44.210 --> 00:07:49.330
through an opening door firing a gun … as
she carried the sequence on, she rushed into

00:07:49.330 --> 00:07:55.640
a corner piece of a set and bumped her head."
The injury left a permanent mark, or so they

00:07:55.640 --> 00:07:57.790
say. Not that anyone can tell.

00:07:57.790 --> 00:07:59.720
Daniel Craig in Spectre

00:07:59.720 --> 00:08:03.820
British actor Daniel Craig's time playing
James Bond has left him with his fair share

00:08:03.820 --> 00:08:09.650
of injuries, as the stunts became more elaborate
with each film. In Casino Royale, two of his

00:08:09.650 --> 00:08:14.220
teeth were accidentally knocked out during
his first stunt and had to be capped, and

00:08:14.220 --> 00:08:18.810
in Quantum of Solace, he suffered several
injuries. There was a blow to his face that

00:08:18.810 --> 00:08:23.590
required plastic surgery, and he was rushed
to hospital after slicing off the top of his

00:08:23.590 --> 00:08:29.050
finger. He also tore a muscle in his shoulder,
and suffered badly bruised ribs.

00:08:29.050 --> 00:08:33.870
But it was Craig's time on Spectre that did
some permanent damage. While filming a fight

00:08:33.870 --> 00:08:38.560
scene with the hulking villain Mr. Hinx, he
injured his knee. It required surgery and

00:08:38.560 --> 00:08:43.210
threatened to halt filming for six months,
but Craig didn't want to wait and put off

00:08:43.210 --> 00:08:46.700
the surgery, working through the pain. He
told Empire,

00:08:46.700 --> 00:08:51.890
"This has been a two-year process since we
began talking about the script. It gets to

00:08:51.890 --> 00:08:56.420
this point and you say: 'We can shut down
for six months and you can go have surgery

00:08:56.420 --> 00:09:02.280
and come back then.' I was like: "F— that."
I don't give a f—. Stick two planks of wood

00:09:02.280 --> 00:09:04.900
on it and I'll f—ing crack on."

00:09:04.900 --> 00:09:09.830
Crack on he did, and in the end, production
was stopped for only two weeks. Craig has

00:09:09.830 --> 00:09:15.390
since had a few surgeries to repair his knee,
and has joked he'll only keep playing 007

00:09:15.390 --> 00:09:17.370
as long as his knees hold out.

00:09:17.370 --> 00:09:20.090
Jackie Chan in...basically all of his movies

00:09:20.090 --> 00:09:25.890
Kung Fu legend Jackie Chan has never held
back and views any injury he sustains while

00:09:25.890 --> 00:09:31.230
filming a stunt as just part of the gig. It's
the one reasons Chan is considered a true

00:09:31.230 --> 00:09:33.680
hero of the martial arts genre.

00:09:33.680 --> 00:09:35.060
"I hear the crack"

00:09:35.060 --> 00:09:37.980
"I look at my feet. Upside down"

00:09:40.320 --> 00:09:41.580
"Then the cameraman, 'Are you OK?'"

00:09:42.020 --> 00:09:44.020
"I'm OK, did you get the shot?"

00:09:44.030 --> 00:09:48.700
He's broken fingers, his nose, ankles, his
tailbone, even his hip; he's dislocated his

00:09:48.700 --> 00:09:54.060
shoulders more than few times and suffered
multiple concussions and spinal injuries.

00:09:54.060 --> 00:09:56.910
The injury list is as long as his resume.

00:09:56.910 --> 00:10:02.260
However, there's one particularly serious
boo-boo that made a lasting impression on

00:10:02.260 --> 00:10:07.400
his banged-up body. During the shoot for Armour
of God , he was supposed to do what was a

00:10:07.400 --> 00:10:13.990
"simple" stunt jump, but he was so hurt by
the maneuver that he had to have brain surgery

00:10:13.990 --> 00:10:18.610
which included the permanent implantation
of a metal plate.

00:10:18.610 --> 00:10:24.990
Even so, Chan's movie momentum, and commitment
to doing his own stunt work, has never wavered.

00:10:24.990 --> 00:10:26.420
Chan's the champ!

00:10:26.420 --> 00:10:30.750
Thanks for watching! Click the Looper icon
to subscribe to our YouTube channel. Plus

00:10:30.750 --> 00:10:33.310
check out all this cool stuff we know you'll
love, too!

